  "details": "Let me explain how this works.\nWhen someone loads in your world VRChat will **locally** load the avatar to calculate the avatar stats of it. This means any normal or crasher avatar will be loaded in even if you have your safety setup to show no avatar at all.\nThis means any crasher avatar can just crash you the moment they load in this avatar without you knowing who it is?!\nThe avatar stats aren't saved in the database or in any json format to receive. It's just get calculate every single time (also performance heavy to do this in the first place).\n(There is nothing in the VRChat API that would show this 'avatar stats')\nCorrect me if I am wrong but I got multiple times that I am chilling with friends someone joins the world and everyone crashes/laggs/game freezes even if no one is friends with them or have them shown...\nReporting is **impossible** when you dont know who just joined if your crashing.",
